<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian cocoa exports fall sharply in May.</title>
<headline>Nigerian cocoa exports fall sharply in May.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cocoa bean exports from Nigeria fell to 861 tonnes in May from 5,994 tonnes a year earlier, official data from the Federal Produce Inspection Agency showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cumulative exports for the first eight months of the 1996/97 (Oct-Sept) year totalled 126,324 tonnes, against 112,644 tonnes by the end of May 1996, the data showed.</p>
<p>Total exports for the 1995/96 season reached 139,063 tonnes, according to official data.</p>
<p>Nigeria's cocoa exports have declined from 300,000 tonnes a year in the early 1970s when attention turned from agriculture to oil. In the long term, buyers say exports will decline further unless ageing trees on peasant smallholdings are replaced.</p>
<p>-- Matthew Tostevin, Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317</p>
</text>
